  "notes": "Atlanta's D.A.R.P. board — new jack swing debut records moving into jazzier sample-soul, 1990–2004. The band is \"86–106 straight; ballads 73–93\", mode 96, the sourced tempo of the C-minor record. Three drum deltas quote the entry: \"the signature is a **'heavy beat' under a light sample**\", which is a `velocityTiers` spread with the accent at 118–127 over an 82–98 main — the widest accent-to-main gap among the producers here, because that is what \"heavy beat, light sample\" is as a parameter; \"kick on 1 and the 16th before 3\" puts the secondary anchor on `2a`; and \"scratching as a percussion layer\" is a `perc`-led four-lane bed at two to five hits a bar. \"The early records use NJS swung 16ths\", so `swing.amount` is 0.59 with `quantizeStrength` at 0.66 — he plays drums as well as keys, and the grid is not tight. Harmony is his identifying move: \"a **'wafting late-night trumpet sample'** as the hook instrument over a minor vamp\", with funk guitar and Rhodes elsewhere, on \"two- and four-bar loops\" — so the counter carries the hook at a 0.5 density with `answer_lick` leading, the families are minor two- and three-chord, and the extension spread is seventh-and-ninth heavy because he was documented taking the material \"darker, mellower, and far jazzier\". The bass is \"synth bass locked to the loop root with a plucked attack\", with \"a quietly jiggling funk guitar\" occupying the register a riffing bass would — so `mirror_kick` at a 0.92 root follow, deliberately unbusy, and no `bass808` block. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is part-sourced: the entry names `Cm`, and the remaining values `Bbm`, `Fm`, `Gm`, together with all 4 weights, are INFERRED rather than read from the entry.",
